So far we have discussed the evaluation of the integrals multiplying $Re_c$ in Eq.~\eqref{Inertial-part}. The three terms multiplying $Re_a$ have the same form and so the same steps apply, except for term $\mathbb{N}_4$. Because the expressions for $\hat{u}_a$ and $w_a$ are lengthier than those for $\hat{u}_a$ and $w_a$, the integral $\mathbb{N}_4$ requires special treatment that was not needed for $\mathbb{N}_3$ (else the integration takes a very long time).
The integrand of $\mathbb{N}_4$ is split into several partial fractions which are integrated individually and then recombined.   
\begin{lstlisting}
dua_dr = sp.diff(u_a,r)
In3_a_fun = sp.expand(v_a*dua_dr*w_a*r)
## splitting
