\begin{abstract}
In our previous work, we defined a prime walk on a square grid and presented several intriguing numerical results. Here, we demonstrate the main conjecture presented there, namely, that the area covered by the prime walk is unbounded. Taking this fact into account, we examine in further detail the properties of the PW and explore new questions that arise naturally in this analysis.
\end{abstract}

