During preprocessing, all images were normalized and resized to (380x380) or (384x384) depending on the~model architecture being trained. In our work, we used only the~types of data augmentation that made the~lungs fully visible after the~transformations, for example, randomly shifting (max. 5\%), scaling (max. 5\%), rotating (max. 15\textdegree), adding noise, and distortion. In~Fig.~\ref{fig:losschannels}, the results show the~higher performance obtained by models with our 3-channel initialization procedure.



