M^{(0)}(n) \cong e n! /n
.
\label{Mn-asymp}
\end{equation} 
%%
Furthermore, inspecting the lists $K^{(0)}(n)$ for $n \leq 8$, equations~\eq{330} and \eq{a10}, we notice that the difference between the largest degree $M^{(0)}(n)$ and the second largest degree $\widetilde{M}^{(0)}(n)$ satisfies 
