\subsection{Structure of Earnings Conference Call}
An earnings conference call typically contains four sections: an introduction from the operator and the executive host, an opening section from the executive presenter, QnA between analysts and the executive presenter, and some closing address from the executive host and the operator. 

\subsubsection{Introduction Section}
The introduction opens with the operator’s welcome and call logistics, then the executive host thanks participants, introduces the leadership team, references the posted earnings release, and hands the presentation over to the CEO. Figure \ref{fig:618492_introduction_text} shows the introduction section for transcript 618492.

