It suffices to show that $J_{131}$$\overset{p}{\rightarrow}0.$ Recall the expression of $F$, i.e. $F=\sum_{j=1}^{N}f_{j}e_{j}^{'}=F_{j}+f_{j}e_{j}^{'}$ where $F_{j}=\sum_{i\neq j}^{N}f_{i}e_{i}^{'}$ and $Z^{'}=\Sigma^{1/2}F.$ By a direct expansion,
