The partition function $Z[\bar{\bm W}]$ defines the aNBK Bayes posterior over the target-task parameters $\bm \theta = \{ \W, \w \}$ at a given source weight $\bar{\bm W}$
\begin{equation}\label{eq::partition_func}
    Z[\bar{\bm W}] = \int d\bm \theta \,\exp \left(-\frac{\beta N \gamma_0^2}{2}\sum_{\mu = 1}^{P_2}\mathcal{L}(\bm \theta, \mathcal{T}_2)-\frac{\lambda}{2}||\bm \theta ||^2 -\frac{\delta}{2}||\bm W - \bar{\bm W}||^2 \right).
