\subsection{Tunable Detection for Safety-Critical Applications}

The reported precision (78.4\%) and recall (81.7\%) represent one operating point on the ROC curve optimized for balanced performance. However, practitioners can adjust detection thresholds to meet specific deployment requirements. Figure~\ref{fig:roc_curves} illustrates this flexibility: by increasing the confidence threshold from 0.6 to 0.8, precision can be improved to approximately 85-90\% at the cost of reducing recall to 65-70\%. This trade-off is particularly valuable in safety-critical applications where false alarms are costly.

For production deployment, we recommend threshold selection based on the relative costs of false positives (unnecessary interventions) versus false negatives (undetected hacking). In autonomous systems, higher precision thresholds minimize disruptive false alarms, while in financial applications, higher recall thresholds ensure comprehensive fraud detection. Our framework's ROC curves enable practitioners to make informed threshold decisions based on their specific risk tolerance and operational constraints.

\subsection{Advanced Detection Techniques}

Beyond the core detectors, we developed several advanced techniques that contribute to our superior performance over existing methods:

\textbf{Multi-Scale Temporal Analysis}: Our specification gaming detector operates at three temporal scales: episode-level (full trajectory analysis), segment-level (sliding windows of 50 timesteps), and transition-level (immediate reward-action correlations). This multi-scale approach captures both persistent and transient hacking behaviors, improving recall by 12.3\% over single-scale methods.

\textbf{Ensemble Calibration}: We employ Platt scaling~\cite{platt1999probabilistic} to calibrate individual detector confidence scores before ensemble combination. This calibration improves the reliability of the ensemble's probability estimates, reducing Brier score from 0.23 to 0.18 and enabling more informed threshold selection.

\textbf{Context-Aware Feature Engineering}: Our detectors incorporate environment-specific features: discrete action spaces use n-gram entropy measures, continuous control tasks use trajectory smoothness metrics, and multi-agent environments include coordination indicators. This context awareness improves F1-scores by 8.7\% compared to generic feature sets.

