Several features of this table are worth noting.  First, both symmetric harmonicity and harmonicity do a fairly good job of reproducing the empirical rankings, especially for the highest-ranked chords; this is certainly a valuable sanity check.  Furthermore, the surprising behavior of Stolzenburg's harmonicity noted in Table~\ref{tab:averageStolzenburg} disappears when we avoid averaging over different translations.  This, to us, further emphasizes the advantage of building translation-invariance (as well as the other types of invariance discussed in this work) directly into the theory, rather than relying on averaging to achieve it.

