The following is well known; see~\cite{Brown1962b}, for example.
\begin{lem}\label{lem:exhaust}
If $W$ is a smooth or topological $n$--manifold, 
then there exists a sequence of compact $n$--manifolds $\{C_i\}_{i\in\omega}$ such that
\[W=\overline{\bigcup_{i\in\omega} C_i}\] and such that \[C_i\sse\inte C_{i+1}\] for all $i$.
