\subsection{Full LLM Judge Evaluation Results}
Confident in the LLM judge's alignment for this task, we proceeded with a full evaluation across 250 test samples derived from the \datasetname dataset interactions. The \texttt{o3-mini} judge produced a 1st, 2nd, and 3rd place ranking for the three models (Qwen, LTU, MU-LLaMA) for every sample prompt. The aggregated performance metrics derived from these rankings are presented in Table \ref{tab:llm_full_results}.



The results indicate that the fine-tuned Qwen model consistently outperformed the other models, achieving the highest number of Rank 1 placements and the best average rank. LTU performed competitively, securing the second position, while MU-LLaMA significantly lagged behind, being ranked last in 76.0\% of the samples.

